Description: RPBridge USB multi-bus bridge kernel driver (Rust, DKMS)
 RPBridge is an open-source USB-to-multi-bus developer tool built on the
 Raspberry Pi RP2354B. The bridge exposes I²C, SPI, UART, GPIO, PWM, ADC
 and CAN 2.0B to a Linux host as standard subsystem devices, usable with
 stock tools (i2c-tools, libgpiod, can-utils, spidev_test, iio_info).
 .
 This package ships the Linux kernel driver source (Rust-for-Linux) and
 integrates it with DKMS so the module is rebuilt automatically on
 kernel upgrades. A kernel with CONFIG_RUST=y is required.
